  <p>
    <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Ocean tides are created by differential gravitational forces from the Moon and
    Sun. These forces don't just move water—they affect Earth's rotation, the Moon's orbit, and create dramatic
    effects throughout the solar system. Tides connect us to the cosmic dance of gravitational interactions that
    shape our world.
  </p>
